WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:13.625
The City of Calgary operates on a five-point-seven billion dollar annual budget, yet its flagship Green Line LRT project has been cut three times while ballooning to four-point-nine billion dollars — with not a single metre of track laid after a decade of planning.

00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:26.488
Mayor Gondek's campaign received significant development industry funding while presiding over cumulative property tax increases exceeding thirty percent, and the Chief Administrative Officer draws four hundred and fifty-four thousand dollars annually.

00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:34.772
When the oil capital of Canada can't build a train line but can pay its executives half a million dollars, the question isn't competence — it's priorities.
